---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms & Conditions | The PC Project" description="Orders, quotes, returns, and Australian Consumer Law for The PC Project.">
  <PageHero label="The-Fine-Print.//" heading="Terms & Conditions">
    <p>By buying from us, booking a build, or using our services, you agree to these terms. They sit alongside your rights under the Australian Consumer Law.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 px-4 pb-24 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/80 sm:px-6">
    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Services</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">We build custom PCs, sell pre-built systems, consult on parts, and do tech support and upgrades. Work follows the spec you approve.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Orders, quotes &amp; payments</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>A configurator submission is a quote request, not an order.</li>
        <li>Quotes are valid for 7 days — hardware prices move.</li>
        <li>A deposit may be required before we order parts or start a custom build.</li>
        <li>Full payment must clear before collection or delivery. We do not hand over a machine until then.</li>
        <li>Build fee is a flat $50 unless we agree otherwise in writing.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Parts</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Parts are new unless we mark them QA Approved. Manufacturer warranties apply to those parts. QA Approved parts are inspected and tested by us before sale or install.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Warranty</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Cover is the Zero-Failure Initiative program. Full detail is on the <a class="text-accent hover:text-paper" href="/warranty-and-returns">Warranty &amp; Returns</a> page.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Returns &amp; refunds</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Report returns within 48 hours of receiving the order. Approved refunds go back to the original payment method. Because builds are custom, change-of-mind returns are not accepted once assembly has started. That does not cut your Australian Consumer Law rights. We assess returned goods before a refund is processed.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Delivery</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">You are responsible for accurate delivery details and safe receipt. Times vary with part availability. Risk passes on collection or confirmed delivery.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Data</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">We use contact details to quote, build, and support the job. Back up your data before you leave a machine with us. We do not keep your files unless the job requires it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">To the maximum extent permitted by law we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, data loss, downtime, or lost income, including from hardware failure. Nothing here excludes or limits Australian Consumer Law. Advice is based on what you tell us and what is in stock; the final spec is your call.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">We are not liable for delay caused by things outside our control, including supply shortages and shipping delays.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-paper">Questions</h2>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="text-accent hover:text-paper" href="mailto:contact@thepcproject.com.au">contact@thepcproject.com.au</a> · 2/62 Fitzgerald Street, Northbridge WA 6003</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
